concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-36 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36 Fabricating evidence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-36 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person:  (i) fabricates evidence; or  (ii) makes use of fabricated evidence; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            15  (b) the person does so with the intention of misleading a court or judicial tribunal in a judicial proceeding; and  (c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person:  (i) fabricates evidence; or  (ii) makes use of fabricated evidence; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            15  (b) the person does so with the intention of misleading a court or judicial tribunal in a judicial proceeding; and  (c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c5414b0437b09fb10a0edc47990c3812e2f9543f285a2abcb60b1ef430915258" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-36-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-36-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf> ;
    dc:source "law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf, p.18" .
doc:sch-2-sec-36 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "36 Fabricating evidence" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person:  (i) fabricates evidence; or  (ii) makes use of fabricated evidence; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            15  (b) the person does so with the intention of misleading a court or judicial tribunal in a judicial proceeding; and  (c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

