doc:sch-2-sec-38-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "38(1) Deceiving witnesses" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            17  (i) practises any fraud or deceit to a person called, or to be called, as a witness in a judicial proceeding; or  (ii) makes or exhibits any false statement, representation, token or writing to a person called, or to be called, as a witness in a judicial proceeding; and  (b) the first person does so with the intention of affecting the testimony of the other person; and  (c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-38-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "38(2) Deceiving witnesses"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-38-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c3c1296a99f77543341be959325bdd056bbf40652784ed90f403c0f4bab98884" ;
    values:partOf concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-38 ;
