concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-14-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14 Subsections 42(1) and (2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-14-2 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            19  (a) the person conspires with another person to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to defeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and  (b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the Commonwealth. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) A person commits an offence if: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            19  (a) the person conspires with another person to obstruct, to prevent, to pervert or to defeat the course of justice in relation to a judicial power; and  (b) the judicial power is the judicial power of the Commonwealth. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-14-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-14-2-ss-2 ;
