concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-44 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44 Compounding offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-44 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) asks for, receives or obtains any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; or  (ii) agrees to receive or to obtain any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; and  (b) the first person does so upon an agreement or understanding that the first person will:  (i) compound or conceal an offence; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Schedule 2  Administration of justice offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) asks for, receives or obtains any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; or  (ii) agrees to receive or to obtain any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; and  (b) the first person does so upon an agreement or understanding that the first person will:  (i) compound or conceal an offence; or ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Schedule 2  Administration of justice offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "445b60e3d67d9709126d248c8ebaaffc6b5e1e507aa3248afd157310b3e16723" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Compounding offences is prohibited" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf> ;
