doc:sch-2-sec-45 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45 Inserting advertisements without authority of court" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person inserts in the Gazette, or in a newspaper, an advertisement purporting to be published under the authority of a court; and  (b) the person does so:  (i) without authority; or  (ii) knowing the advertisement to be false in any material particular; and  (c) the advertisement purports to be published under the authority of:  (i) a federal court; or  (ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or  (iii) a court of a Territory. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

