concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-47 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47 Escaping"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-47 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is in criminal detention; and  (b) the person escapes from that detention; and  (c) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            23 Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is in criminal detention; and  (b) the person escapes from that detention; and  (c) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Administration of justice offences  Schedule 2 Amendment of the Crimes Act 1914  Part 1  Law and Justice Legislation Amendment (Identity Crimes and Other Measures) Act 2011       No. 3, 2011            23 Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9e2844d8376f6310645f5e811c7f9d9a36a5155d35a24c754d0ebc6a42cba9c4" ;
