concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-47a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47A Rescuing a prisoner from criminal detention"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-47a ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) another person (the prisoner) is in criminal detention; and  (b) the first person rescues the prisoner from that detention by force; and  (c) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention. Penalty: Imprisonment for 14 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) another person (the prisoner) is in criminal detention; and  (b) the first person rescues the prisoner from that detention by force; and  (c) the detention is lawful federal criminal detention. Penalty: Imprisonment for 14 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
