concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49 Removing property under seizure"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-49 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or authority of a court; and  (b) the court was:  (i) a federal court; or  (ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or  (iii) a court of a Territory; and  (c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of the property; and  (d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or defeating the attachment or process. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Schedule 2  Administration of justice offences" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or authority of a court; and  (b) the court was:  (i) a federal court; or  (ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or  (iii) a court of a Territory; and  (c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of the property; and  (d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or defeating the attachment or process. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Schedule 2  Administration of justice offences"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e1891380dbd6e62aeacbb4438105281822afc146612734f426c78e7033f9d289" ;
    cof:pageNumber "29"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-49-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
