concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-2-sec-23 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23 Section 183"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-23 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the section, substitute: 183  Aiding persons to escape etc.  Sections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have effect as if:  (a) arrest pursuant to this Act were arrest in respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth; and  (b) custody while in Australia pursuant to this Act were custody in respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth. International Transfer of Prisoners Act 1997" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the section, substitute: 183  Aiding persons to escape etc.  Sections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have effect as if:  (a) arrest pursuant to this Act were arrest in respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth; and  (b) custody while in Australia pursuant to this Act were custody in respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth. International Transfer of Prisoners Act 1997"@en ;
