concept:law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011-sch-3-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 After subsection 31(1A)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "Insert:  (1B) The Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate to:  (a) a person performing a similar role under a law of a State or Territory; or  (b) a member of the staff of a State or Territory authority (within the meaning of subsection 15(3)) who is a legal practitioner; or  (c) a person authorised by, or under, a law of a State or Territory to institute or conduct prosecutions for offences against the laws of the State or Territory; or  (d) a person included in a class of persons prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph; all or any of the Director’s functions and powers under the following provisions:  (e) paragraphs 6(1)(a), (b), (c), (d) and (e);  (f) paragraph 6(1)(n) (so far as it relates to the functions covered by paragraph (e) of this subsection); ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Schedule 3  Director of Public Prosecutions Act 1983" ;
    skos:definition "Insert:  (1B) The Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate to:  (a) a person performing a similar role under a law of a State or Territory; or  (b) a member of the staff of a State or Territory authority (within the meaning of subsection 15(3)) who is a legal practitioner; or  (c) a person authorised by, or under, a law of a State or Territory to institute or conduct prosecutions for offences against the laws of the State or Territory; or  (d) a person included in a class of persons prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph; all or any of the Director’s functions and powers under the following provisions:  (e) paragraphs 6(1)(a), (b), (c), (d) and (e);  (f) paragraph 6(1)(n) (so far as it relates to the functions covered by paragraph (e) of this subsection); ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00003  Schedule 3  Director of Public Prosecutions Act 1983"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bbcbfb7d5d093dd2d971ea27604158dcac75a513d56b24fef5d863a88cbe2d70" ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Director may delegate functions and powers to certain persons or authorities." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <law-and-justice-legislation-amendment-identity-crimes-and-other-measures-act-2011.pdf> ;
